  "document": "Congo–Ocean Railway\nThe Congo–Ocean Railway (COR; French: \"Chemin de fer Congo-Océan\" , CFCO ) links the Atlantic port of Pointe-Noire (now in the Republic of Congo) with Brazzaville, a distance of 502 km . It bypasses the rapids on the lower Congo River; from Brazzaville river boats are able to ascend the Congo River and its major tributaries, including the Oubangui River to Bangui."
